    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Commands, and the gate set",
      "prov:value": "The commands are listed in [`README.md`](README.md#running-it). Two are worth an agent's attention. **`bun run cat gates` before you push** — it derives its list from `.github/workflows/code-quality-gates.yml`, and **a subset of the gate set is not the gate set** ([`platform-gates`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/platform-gates.md)). **`bun run cat preview:site`**, because a green gate set is not a rendered page ([`rendered-verification`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-verification.md), bean `gjli`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean gjli"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the harness keeps its state",
      "prov:value": "`beans/` is a graph with named nodes, declared by `beans/beans.json` (schema `schemas/sdlc/bean-graph.ts`), and a file declares what it is: a bean by its front matter, a workflow instance by `\"$schema\": \"folio-workflow-instance/v1\"`. **Extension is a coincidence; a declaration inside the file is the contract.** The two duplicates of the layout that cannot be removed are both checked by `bun run cat check:harness-dirs`: `.beans.yml`, because the `beans` binary is third-party, and `WORKFLOW_DIR` in `src/workflow/store.ts`, because it is on the hot path of every workflow call. These were `.beans/` and `.harness/workflow/` until 2026-09-18 (beans `8xzw`, `x89g`), and `.harness/` is gone — a dot-prefixed path is what this layer's own guard rejects. The tracked graphs are kept on state branches now and mounted by the session-start hook (`bun run cat state:mount`). QA verdicts are on the orphan `qa-reports` branch; judgements stay in `test/attestations/` ([`directory-conventions`](skills/kg/kg-core/directory-conventions.md), [`workflow-state`](skills/process/workflow/workflow-state.md), [`qa-reports`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-reports.md), [the proposal](docs/proposals/workflow-state-in-beans.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-18",
        "bean 8xzw",
        "bean x89g",
        "docs/proposals/workflow-state-in-beans.md"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "CI health, repository health and audit coverage",
      "prov:value": "Three questions, three commands. **`bun run cat check:ci-health`** — do the workflows pass, and are the Pages previews building ([`ci-health`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md); one workflow failed all 30 times over two months with nothing saying so, bean `xom7`). Do not \"fix\" a dispatch-only workflow by dispatching it ([`memory/`](memory/two-workflows-fail-by-design-here-do-not-fix-them-by-dispatc.md)). **`bun run cat health`** — the repository itself: how much of the publish branch the previews occupy, what a clone costs, whether the work plan has duplicates or unhonoured claims. Its checks are in `test/health/`, `health:list` names them, and every threshold carries its **basis**. The same three rules as CI health hold — could-not-determine is never clean, the tracking issue is edited in place, and on `unknown` it is left untouched while the job fails — and **it reports and never acts**: every finding's action is a person's ([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md), bean `plj1`). **`bun run cat audit:coverage`** — what is audited at all, per graph typology ([`audit-coverage`](skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean xom7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "CI health, repository health and audit coverage",
      "prov:value": "Three questions, three commands. **`bun run cat check:ci-health`** — do the workflows pass, and are the Pages previews building ([`ci-health`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md); one workflow failed all 30 times over two months with nothing saying so, bean `xom7`). Do not \"fix\" a dispatch-only workflow by dispatching it ([`memory/`](memory/two-workflows-fail-by-design-here-do-not-fix-them-by-dispatc.md)). **`bun run cat health`** — the repository itself: how much of the publish branch the previews occupy, what a clone costs, whether the work plan has duplicates or unhonoured claims. Its checks are in `test/health/`, `health:list` names them, and every threshold carries its **basis**. The same three rules as CI health hold — could-not-determine is never clean, the tracking issue is edited in place, and on `unknown` it is left untouched while the job fails — and **it reports and never acts**: every finding's action is a person's ([`deletion-requires-confirmation`](skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md), bean `plj1`). **`bun run cat audit:coverage`** — what is audited at all, per graph typology ([`audit-coverage`](skills/kg/kg-core/audit-coverage.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean plj1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "More",
      "prov:value": "- **Not sure where a thing goes?** [`where-does-this-go`](skills/conduct/conduct-core/where-does-this-go.md), and its companion [`surprise-to-corpus`](skills/kg/kg-core/surprise-to-corpus.md). - **`uses[]` and `interprets` are the EDITORIAL relation** — never populate `uses[]` from Lean. Contract: `BlockBase.uses` and `RemarkBlock.interprets` in `schemas/types.ts` ([`uses-editorial-review`](skills/authoring/authoring-core/uses-editorial-review.md)). - **Every process is BPMN, and the diagrams are executable** ([`bpmn-processes`](skills/process/workflow/bpmn-processes.md), [`workflow-state`](skills/process/workflow/workflow-state.md), [the publication-workflow page](https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/folio-assistant-core/process/publication-workflow.html)). `bun run cat render:bpmn` regenerates the pictures. - **Process state, blocking and swarms** — [`process-state`](skills/process/workflow/process-state.md), [`bean-blocking`](work-plan/skills/work-plan/bean-blocking.md), [`swarm-management`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/swarm-management.md). - **An instance declares the directories it scans** in `<instance>.json`, each with the kind of graph it holds; overrides match on the entry's `id`, not its `path`, and only what exists is declared ([`content-context-and-state-graphs`](skills/kg/kg-core/content-context-and-state-graphs.md), [`directory-conventions`](skills/kg/kg-core/directory-conventions.md)). `cat-harness.json` is the list — not a sentence anywhere. - **Adding a skill is never a one-file change** — `bun run cat skill:register` ([`skill-registration`](skills/kg/kg-core/skill-registration.md)). - **Shipping a branch** — [`prepare-merge`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/prepare-merge.md); **watching a sibling PR** — [`watch`](sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/watch.md). - **Migration plan and cross-repo coordination** — [`docs/folio-assistant-migration.md`](docs/folio-assistant-migration.md); the Lean tooling roadmap is issue #198. - **The generated references are never hand-edited**: regenerate them with `bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/gen-schema-docs.ts` and `bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/gen-skill-docs.ts`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#198"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "(footer)",
      "prov:value": "*A declared asset of this instance ([`cat-harness.json`](cat-harness.json), role `agent-instructions`). Authored here — it is not a copy of [`bootstrap/AGENTS.md`](../bootstrap/AGENTS.md). The checkout root's `AGENTS.md` quotes that file as its cold start, and is rendered rather than declared (`scripts/index-render.ts`). Issue #592.*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#592"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "AGENTS.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Feature requests and CRDM",
      "prov:value": "A feature request enters the CRDM requirements workflow rather than being implemented directly ([`crdm-detect`](sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-detect.md), [`crdm-requirements-workflow`](sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md), [the methodology](docs/process/crdm-methodology.md)). **The process is executable — do not hand-roll a phase tracker**: `workflow_start` / `workflow_next` / `workflow_complete` run it, and `crdm_start` / `crdm_status` should not be built. The interaction model as a whole is [the agentic harness page](docs/concepts/agentic-harness.md)."
    }
  ]
